import{_ as t,o as s,c as a,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.BUOFcz_J.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Agent activity in Rho","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"concepts/agent-activity.md","filePath":"concepts/agent-activity.md"}'),n={name:"concepts/agent-activity.md"};function o(r,e,d,c,l,h){return s(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i(`<h1 id="agent-activity-in-rho" tabindex="-1">Agent activity in Rho <a class="header-anchor" href="#agent-activity-in-rho" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Agent activity in Rho&quot;">​</a></h1><p><strong>Activity from the project Host</strong>, at the foot of the Agent page&#39;s Outside Rho tab, shows selected Claude Code and dsh observations retained by Core; it is read only while open, and opening it brings it into view. It shows tool requests, corresponding returns, refusals, native exit codes and output files. External sessions keep their input in their original window; opening this view sends no message and starts no Agent or Host.</p><h2 id="connect-an-existing-session" tabindex="-1">Connect an existing session <a class="header-anchor" href="#connect-an-existing-session" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Connect an existing session&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Select an activity-capable Core build and the Agent collector described in <a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho-plugins/blob/main/examples/agent-observation/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">the owner guide</a>. The application selects Agent 0.4.15 and Tables 0.4.3. Core state format 4 is required for this stream; old state is refused intact. Do not replace an existing project&#39;s Host or remove its state to make the view connect.</p><p>Runs 1–6 used Agent 0.4.7 from <a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho-plugins/commit/0a7551617299f6c7464c79a5e1904ac7d2d32df2" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Plugins 0a755161</a> with <a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho-core/commit/4f5bed8631e15acad44cc86b63ea4779ab8af342" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Core 4f5bed86</a>; runs 7–8 below record theirs.</p><p>Rho reads the project&#39;s existing <code>.rho/host.sock</code>, in the fixed Core caller namespace <code>rho-agent-observe</code>. The operator attaches a collector to that same Host and selects one exact native session:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-light vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#6F42C1;">rho-agent-observe</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> collect</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;">  --core</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> /absolute/rho-core</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;">  --socket</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> /absolute/project/.rho/host.sock</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;">  --caller</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> rho-agent-observe</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> --stream</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> analysis-session</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;">  --producer</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> claude</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> --project</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> /absolute/project</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;">  --session</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> NATIVE_SESSION_ID</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> --source</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> /absolute/session.jsonl</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;">  --watch-seconds</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> 3600</span></span></code></pre></div><p>For dsh, choose <code>--producer dsh</code>, its session storage root for <code>--source</code>, and the installed dsh <code>package.json</code> with <code>--dsh-package</code>. The collector uses dsh&#39;s native read-only persistence API. Native dependencies remain optional. The directory and session are explicit selections; this feature does not scan every session on the machine. Reusing a stream requires its original source and normalization.</p><p>The default captures bounded command/path metadata, call identities and error facts. <code>--content</code> additionally captures bounded tool details after best-effort redaction. It is an operator choice, not a browser switch. Reasoning is excluded. The browser shows captured result details when present and says when they were not captured. Redaction is not a universal secret detector.</p><p>Rho&#39;s existing <a href="/Rho/docs/concepts/execution#host-lifetime">execution bridge</a> governs Host ownership. A fresh disposable project&#39;s Host can be started explicitly with <code>rho-core serve --project /absolute/project --state-dir /absolute/project/.rho</code>. An observation-only Host has no R executor; managed R actions need the selected R executor under the existing lifecycle contract.</p><h2 id="reading-and-opening-results" tabindex="-1">Reading and opening results <a class="header-anchor" href="#reading-and-opening-results" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Reading and opening results&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Choose a session in the section. The view polls retained activity every 1.5 seconds while open. Its connection label describes the observation store, not whether the external Agent or collector is alive. The last receipt time remains visible. A request with no observed return says <strong>Awaiting result</strong>. A successful tool envelope and a nonzero process exit remain separate facts; dsh can report both.</p><p>On a connection failure the view stops polling and keeps its received actions. <strong>Reconnect activity</strong> reads the same stream after its existing cursor. It does not start a Host, restart a collector, submit work or resume a model. Reload can rebuild the view from Core when that Host is available. Closing the page releases its timers and requests only.</p><p>The <strong>Outputs</strong> section observes a chosen project subfolder, initially <code>outputs</code>, every five seconds. It shows current paths, byte counts and SHA-256 prefixes. These files are not automatically attributed to a tool call or declared complete. <strong>Open</strong> checks the exact observed digest and imports a snapshot through Files. Tables opens CSV with every value preserved as text and no invented entity key; Media opens the selected image. Other text files use the live Documents editor, without a captured-version claim. PDF preview is not available here. An updated output requires refreshing its observation. Previously captured versions remain readable. The snapshot source line says <strong>producer unconfirmed</strong>.</p><p>Opening a snapshot inserts an exact resource/version into <code>observed-outputs</code> through the existing conditional composition API. A stale layout is refused; existing protected views are not replaced. Reload retains both output views, using the workspace&#39;s existing initial-tab behavior. Selecting the figure tab reopens the saved version without running the analysis.</p><h2 id="boundaries-and-limits" tabindex="-1">Boundaries and limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#boundaries-and-limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Boundaries and limits&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Rho supplies authentication, project scope, the selected Core transport and layout. Agent owns normalization, projection and the activity view. Tables owns lexical CSV declarations. Files owns captured bytes; Media owns image display.</li><li>Three owner operations, <code>agent.activity.read</code>, <code>agent.activity.outputs</code> and <code>agent.activity.capture</code>, use the normal scoped HTTP contract. Browser scope includes them. They are excluded from default Agent grants, which still fit the existing 64-method profile. No browser can select another Core caller.</li><li>A read page is at most 128 events / 256 KiB; the view retains a suffix of at most 256 events / 1 MiB serialized JSON. Core gaps and view eviction are visible. Missing request/return evidence stays incomplete. These are serialized budgets, not an OS heap guarantee.</li><li>Output scans retain the owner&#39;s limits: 64 files, 256 directory entries, depth 4 and 8 MiB per file. Symlinks are skipped or refused. Internal <code>.rho</code> and <code>.git</code> paths and parent traversal are refused. Scan failures preserve the previous displayed observation; changing folders clears the previous folder.</li><li>Core history, collector progress, artifact integrity, execution and scientific interpretation remain separate. Workspace archives do not archive the native Agent session or this Core activity stream. No native execution deduplication, universal monitoring, model understanding or scientific validity is claimed.</li></ul><h2 id="real-episode-and-review" tabindex="-1">Real episode and review <a class="header-anchor" href="#real-episode-and-review" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Real episode and review&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Run from the source checkout with the selected clients and gateway configuration:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-light vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#24292E;">RHO_CORE_BINARY</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#D73A49;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;">/absolute/rho-core</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#6F42C1;"> npm</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> run</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> acceptance:agent-activity</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The harness creates disposable projects and private client configurations. Both clients explicitly select <code>westlakehpc/deepseek-v4.1-flash</code>. Each reads a six-row CSV, fixes integer division in a Python group mean, then executes the analysis once. An explicit fixture gate lets the browser observe the pending request. The harness stops its collector and kills only its owned Host; the original Agent continues, writes CSV/SVG and exits the tool with diagnostic code 7. Reattachment backfills that same session. Browser checks open the actual table and figure, inspect 1440/390-pixel widths and reopen retained views after reload. An independent calculation checks the two means, 11/3 and 8/3. These arithmetic checks do not establish a scientific method or human usability.</p><p>Iteration evidence is retained under <code>work/agent-activity/</code>:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Run</th><th>Observed result and decision</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1, Claude</td><td>Live pending, Host loss, error and recovery worked. A test treated an overflow boolean as an array and stopped. The screen buried outputs beneath the action list; the view now places outputs alongside a bounded scrolling list on a wide screen.</td></tr><tr><td>2, Claude</td><td>The model added a shell suffix, received a native permission refusal and did not execute the analysis. The fixture timed out. The test prompt now explicitly requires the exact command.</td></tr><tr><td>3, Claude</td><td>Live/recovery/error checks passed. Opening exposed an invalid workspace ID containing a space. Rho now uses <code>observed-outputs</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>4, dsh</td><td>Live/recovery/error checks and actual table opening worked; an obsolete <code>.ag-body</code> selector stopped the harness. It now reads the actual grid root.</td></tr><tr><td>5, dsh</td><td>The table and decoded SVG opened. Reload restored both tabs but selected the first, the existing workspace behavior. The check now explicitly reopens the retained figure tab rather than asserting an unimplemented active-tab restore.</td></tr><tr><td>6, both</td><td>Both full flows passed: pending calls, retained actions during disconnection, same-session recovery, diagnostic exit 7, table/image opening and reload. Each analysis ran once; repeat collection appended zero events.</td></tr><tr><td>7, both (2026-10-28)</td><td>The cards of Agent 0.4.14 under Outside Rho. Both flows passed (Claude Code 2.1.312: 7 then 10 events; dsh 0.2.1-rc.2: 9 then 18; each analysis once, repeat collection added none, no page errors). Read: the pending and disconnected screenshots showed only the setup steps, because the opened section unfolded below the fold; Read/Edit cards gave absolute paths such as <code>/private/tmp/rho-act-…/claude-activity/analysis.py</code>, two lines at 390 px. Opening the section now scrolls it into view; Agent 0.4.15 shows a path inside the project relative to it.</td></tr><tr><td>8, both</td><td>Same flows passed (9 then 14 and 11 then 18 events, one run each, none added on repeat). The pending action and the Host-lost card are now on the first screen; cards read <code>analysis.py</code> and <code>outputs/summary.csv</code>. A command keeps the path the Agent wrote in it.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Visual review of run 6 covered pending/empty outputs, disconnected actions, recovered errors, the table and decoded SVG at 1440 pixels, plus actions and outputs at 390 pixels. Commands and errors remain readable, the narrow view stacks outputs below the bounded action list, and the two output controls are reachable without horizontal overflow. This is a visual inspection, separate from browser assertions and human usability evidence. A final review corrected the text-file snapshot wording and refuses unsupported PDF preview explicitly. After rebuilding those changes, both retained real sessions passed a browser continuation: errors remained visible, CSV/SVG reopened, repeated Open kept two views, PDF was refused, and each original analysis still had one invocation. <code>work/agent-activity/final-browser-review.json</code> records this later build separately from run 6. The rebuilt owner suite passed 76/76; scoped HTTP and ledger checks passed 3/3. One attempted owner check had used stale compiled files before the owner rebuild; its failure remains in the local evidence.</p><p>Owner checks also exposed that ordinary registration still checks the mutable source file. Activity opening now uses Files&#39; existing snapshot import so that later outside edits cannot invalidate an already opened version. The regression checks old and new snapshots independently. A separate HTTP check verifies the project and caller boundary, missing-Host reads, unchanged default grants and the exact lexical table through the served response schema.</p><p>The final executed results and composition are recorded in <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/status">Status</a>. The local episode report records Core binary/source identities, browser asset hashes, source input hashes and explicit local overrides. This is application integration evidence; source publication, installation and signed distribution have separate scopes in <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/release">Release</a>.</p><p>Runs 7–8 used application <code>becb9373</code>, Plugins <code>078aa074</code> (run 8 with the 0.4.15 change, since committed as <code>977638a</code>) and Core source <code>1e95dd79</code> with Chrome 155; the application checkout also held unrelated untracked files, so both reports mark it locally overridden. Opening scrolls before the first read arrives, so the section lands part-way down rather than at the top. Evidence: <code>work/agent-activity/run-7/</code>, <code>run-8/</code> (ignored by Git). Checks after run 8: Rho 218/218 and Plugins 92/92 (<a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/blob/main/docs/VERIFICATION.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ledger</a>), <code>frontend</code> 13/13, pages at four widths and plugin UI. In that serial batch <code>agent-page</code> met a Codex row still Working and <code>continuity</code> waited over 30 s for Connected after its restart; each passed 7/7 when run again alone.</p>`,27)])])}const g=t(n,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
